Package: trendspull
Title: Collect and Plot Google Trends Timelines
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Maxwell A.", "Konnaris", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "69332438+maxwellkonnaris@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Collect Google Trends timelines through the shared Python
    'trendspull' backend, retain collection metadata and quality flags, compute
    proportions among selected terms, and plot comparable search interest.
    Uses raw joint comparisons for up to five terms and G-TAB calibration for
    larger sets, following West (2020) <doi:10.1145/3340531.3412075>.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: reticulate (>= 1.41), ggplot2 (>= 3.4.0), patchwork (>= 1.1.0), grid, stats, rlang
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.2.0), withr (>= 2.5.0)
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.11), Python packages pandas and requests
URL: https://github.com/maxwellkonnaris/googletrends
BugReports: https://github.com/maxwellkonnaris/googletrends/issues
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
